# T6007 (2026-08-26).  The subdirectories below hold scratch, generated, or
# superseded fixtures that no code path reads -- from a reference sweep
# over crates/, vendor/, scripts/ and data/**/*.py.  (That sweep missed
# test1.bin, which three tracked manifests DO read; it is re-included at
# the bottom of this file.)  They are
# untracked ENTIRELY, so the 4open export omits them; a local working
# tree keeps the files.  Everything else under debug/ IS tracked on
# purpose: this rule dropped 7 of the 24 subdirectories that used to be
# tracked; the 17 that remain are all read by the Rust test suite and
# must stay.
#
# t602_probe_scratch_* are WRITE targets -- probe_t602.rs regenerates them
# via create_smaller_config(), which fs::create_dir_all()s the directory,
# so neither the files nor the folder needs to ship.

full_debug/
gandcrab_repro/
small_debug_set/
small_repro_aggr/
t602_probe_scratch_2000/
t602_probe_scratch_400/
watson_seg5/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# INVARIANT: if a test opens it, it must be TRACKED.  A fresh
# `git archive` export must pass, with no INSTALL.py step, every
# `cargo test` that does not itself require an INSTALL.py-downloaded
# dataset.
#
# These are fixture INPUTS that a blanket rule elsewhere would otherwise
# untrack, making the shipped artifact fail its own test suite while the
# working tree passes (the working tree has them, untracked).  A deeper
# .gitignore overrides the repo root, so these re-include past `*.txt`.
#
#   test1.bin        <- small_data_set/config/binexec.dat:1,
#                       small_data_set2/config/binexec.dat:1,
#                       small_dna/config/binexec.dat:1
#   sed/simple/*.txt <- clam_db.rs build_db_from_dir() reads needs_dfa /
#                       needs_ised / needs_ised_igc; fsm_adv.rs:2439
#                       reads word.txt
#   dfa/simple/*.txt <- same three, plus dfa_adv.rs:1422 word2.txt
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
!test1.bin
!sed/simple/*.txt
!dfa/simple/*.txt
